# .publishing_protocol — per-repo publishing config, read by nao-aur-publish
# and by agents before any release work. Generic rules: PUBLISHING_PROTOCOL.md
# in the nao-aur-publish repo.
PUBLISH_BRANCH=master
PKGBUILD_PATH=PKGBUILD
AUR_PACKAGE=llama-launcher
# NOTES:
# - AUR is published ONLY via: nao-aur-publish llama-launcher vN
#   Never push this repo's git history to AUR.
# - PKGBUILD source= points at Codeberg; the vN tag must be on Codeberg
#   before publishing (nao-aur-publish checks this).
# - .SRCINFO is never committed here — generated at publish time.
#
# Step 0 privacy/malice audit (nao-aur-publish/audit-release.sh):
# SENSITIVE audit values (real names, hostnames, usernames that must never
# ship) live in .publishing_protocol.local — gitignored, local-only, NOT in
# this repo. Rationale: a denylist committed to a public mirror publishes the
# very identifiers it names (2026-08-26: AUDIT_KNOWN_NAMES/HOSTNAMES were
# committed into the v24 chain and had to be rewritten out).
# .publishing_protocol.local format (same key=value lines):
#   AUDIT_KNOWN_NAMES=...
#   AUDIT_HOSTNAMES=...
#   AUDIT_IDENTITY_ALLOW=name|email,...
# If the local file is absent, the audit runs with its built-in defaults
# (no known-names, Lumina identity allowlist) and prints a notice — it does
# NOT block on the missing file.
